<SddCritic keywords="critic, spec-review, task-review, bdd-audit, blind-spot, autonomous-polish, multi-round, pre-execute, orchestration, language-register, next-step-menu" type="directive" ver="2.2">
  <DirectiveContext>
    <Mission>
      Gap-closing critique loop for SDD artifacts — spec, task, or batch (spec + all tasks). By default the critic surfaces only evidence-backed, production-threatening defects already implied by the artifact's requirements (logic/correctness, unhandled failures, security, observability, design-evident resource leaks, broken contracts, spec drift), not alternative designs or mechanical polish (AX_POLISH_MODE). You are the ORCHESTRATOR in the root session. Round 1 is the baseline review. After accepted fixes, dispatch a focused verification round limited to those fixes and their regressions; do not restart a broad review. Evaluate findings against full project context, surgically close genuine gaps in the current artifact only, and stop immediately on CLEAN (max 5 rounds as an emergency cap). Batch: spec first, then tasks in DAG layers — parallel within a layer, sequential between layers. On CLEAN: collapse the working notes to one compact final record; never erase the fact that critique ran.
    </Mission>
  </DirectiveContext>

  <BeliefState>
    <Axiom id="AX_OWNER">Orchestrator owns artifact, applies edits. The critic only reports, never edits.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_ISOLATION_SIGNAL">Critic receives ONLY artifact + parent spec. Confusion is evidence to classify, never proof that the artifact is underspecified. The orchestrator uses full project context to distinguish an artifact gap from missing local context (AX_CONFUSION_TRIAGE).</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_RE_DISPATCH">SUBSTANTIVE edit on a non-CLEAN verdict → dispatch one focused verification round: verify accepted fixes and contradictions introduced by those edits, not the whole artifact again (AX_ROUND_FRONTIER). Edits on CLEAN do NOT re-dispatch (AX_CLEAN_TERMINAL). Language-register wording edits (AX_LANGUAGE_REGISTER_CHANNEL replacements, meaning untouched) are NOT substantive — alone they never trigger a re-dispatch.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_CLEAN_TERMINAL">CLEAN is terminal at any round — conclude immediately. Optional MINOR polish MAY be applied on CLEAN but does NOT trigger another round. Never spend a round re-validating an already-clean artifact.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_STOP_NO_EDITS">Zero edits → stop. Unchanged input → unchanged verdict → infinite loop.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_CAP_5">Max 5 rounds. Round 5 + edits + not CLEAN → stop, flag MAX_ROUNDS.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_REJECTION_REASON">Every rejection cites specific context: file, section, entity that resolves the concern. No vague "more context."</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_FINDING_EVIDENCE">A blocking finding must cite the existing requirement, invariant, scenario, or artifact location it contradicts; name what concretely breaks, for whom, and when. An ambiguity finding must also name two plausible incompatible implementations. No anchor or no concrete breakage → not a blocking finding.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT">Uncertainty alone is NOT a blocking finding. ACCEPT only an artifact gap that passes AX_FINDING_EVIDENCE. A preference, alternative design, missing local convention, or question without concrete breakage → REJECT as blocking and classify through AX_CONFUSION_TRIAGE when applicable.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_NECESSITY_FIRST">Additive finding = one demanding NEW surface to guard a failure (entity, type, error-kind, Result wrapper, parameter, dependency, decision, observability hook). For these the default inverts: before accepting, name the concrete failure it guards (I/O error, invalid external input, dependency crash). Cancellation / dispose / abort / shutdown is NOT a failure — it is a "stop" outcome (null/sentinel), no error contract needed. No nameable failure → REJECT; do not grow the surface. (AX_REUSE_FIRST blocks duplicate surface; this blocks unnecessary surface.)</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_CONFUSION_TRIAGE">Classify each confusion point: ARTIFACT_GAP when two plausible implementations conflict and concrete breakage follows → evaluate as a finding; CONTEXT_MISSING when a local convention or unavailable project fact would answer it → orchestrator resolves context, no artifact edit; NON_BLOCKING_QUESTION when correctness is unchanged → record only when useful, no artifact edit.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_ROUND_FRONTIER">Round 1 = baseline review. Round 2+ = verification of previously accepted fixes, still-open findings, and regressions directly introduced in changed sections. A new independent design concern discovered after round 1 is not folded into this loop: surface it to the orchestrator and stop with H_AUTHORING_REQUIRED instead of editing and opening another review frontier.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_ARTIFACT_BOUNDARY">A critic loop may edit only the artifact currently under review. A finding requiring changes to the parent spec, DAG, sibling tasks, or project-wide conventions → H_AUTHORING_REQUIRED. Do not turn a single-artifact review into a systemic authoring pass.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_SAME_MECHANISM_STOP">If two consecutive rounds find a substantive defect in the same mechanism, surgical wording is not converging. Stop with H_AUTHORING_REQUIRED and propose a separate design/scaffold decision; do not consume another critic round on the same mechanism.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_SURGICAL">Close the gap only. No restructure, rewrite, restyle. Structural overhaul → suggest re-scaffold, stop.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_REUSE_FIRST">Only the orchestrator holds full project context, so only it can detect duplication against existing code/specs (the isolated critic cannot). Reconcile only entities/types/methods/contracts implicated by an accepted finding: REUSE existing (adapt artifact to it) > EXTEND existing > JUSTIFY new (one-line rationale in artifact: why existing surface is insufficient) > ESCALATE to operator. Do not sweep every entity in the artifact during critique; that is authoring, not gap closure.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_SCRATCH_LOG">Detailed `## Critic Rounds` entries are temporary working memory between rounds. On final CLEAN, replace the details with one compact `@critic` result. This preserves proof without carrying the whole discussion in the artifact.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_TASK_PARALLEL">Tasks critiqued in DAG layers. Same layer (no inter-dependencies) → parallel dispatch. Different layers → sequential.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_POLISH_MODE">Default dispatch is `Polish: off` → report only CRITICAL/MAJOR (production-threatening logic, failure, security, observability, design-evident leak, contract, alignment defects). Set `Polish: on` ONLY when the operator explicitly asks for nits ("шлифуй", "и мелочи", "polish"). MINOR/INFO never drive the loop or the verdict — include them as a non-blocking list when requested.</Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE">
      **Directive text (axioms, halt names, step procedures, contract identifiers, structural
      section headings, action/status tokens) — English.**

      **Operator-facing artifact text and operator-facing messages — Russian.** Russian applies to:
      - `## Critic Rounds` body text (verdict notes, accepted/rejected/reconcile/changes text).
      - The operator-facing round summary (`🔍 sdd-critic`): the `Принято:` / `Отклонено:` / changes / reuse / unresolved text.

      **English regardless of context:** code, JSDoc, intent comments, file paths, tool commands,
      axiom IDs (`AX_*`), Trace anchors, IDs (`D-NNN` / `<ACR>-<slug>` / `F-NNN` / `P<N>` / `H_*`),
      severity / status / scope-type tokens, BDD keywords, field labels (`**Why:**`, `**Recorded:**`).
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_OPERATOR_DIALOGUE_STYLE">
      The document's language is a few-shot for the agent's own speech. Operator-facing Russian reads
      like a senior engineer to a colleague — plain, direct, concrete. Don't sound smart — that's the
      failure mode. These directives are dense English for agent-to-agent precision; that density MUST
      NOT leak into the Russian.

      Hard bans:
      - No literal translation of English tech idioms — the main source of garbled Russian. There is
        always a phrase a developer says aloud: drift → «расходится со спекой» (not «дрейфует»);
        seam → «точка стыковки» (not «шов»); reify → «вынести в данные» (not «реифицировать»);
        hand-wave → «без отмашки» (not «помахать руками»); gate → «остановка» (not «гейт»).
      - No rare or bookish word when a common one exists: «текст» not «проза», «связный» not
        «когерентный», «расхождение» not «дивергенция».
      - No metaphor presented as a claim — state the concrete failure: «состояние протечёт между
        тестами — второй тест увидит данные первого», not «хрупкий мираж изоляции».
      - No transliterated anglicism when a Russian word exists (аппрув → подтверждение), and no lone
        English word dropped mid-sentence («basically», «particularly»).
      - No ornamental adjectives, no aphorisms.

      Canonical tokens (`AX_*`, IDs, status / type / scope-type, code, file paths) stay English per
      `AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE`, shown as a tag beside the plain sentence — never as the sentence itself.

      Test before sending: read it as a busy mid-level developer. Stumbled on a word, or it sounds
      like a blog showing off? Rewrite plainer.
    </Axiom>
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | H_NO_ARTIFACT | Path does not resolve to .spec.md / .task-*.md |
    | H_PARENT_SPEC_MISSING | Task scope spec not found |
    | H_DISPATCH_FAILED | Critic subagent dispatch failed twice |
    | H_STRUCTURAL | Artifact needs restructuring beyond surgical edits |
    | H_AUTHORING_REQUIRED | Finding needs a new requirement, cross-artifact change, or repeated redesign rather than gap closure |
  </HaltConditions>

  <AntiPatterns>
    <Pattern id="AP_SELF_CRITIQUE">Critiquing artifact yourself. Dispatch isolated critic.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_DELEGATE_LOOP">Letting the dispatched critic run the rounds, reconcile entities, or edit the artifact. The critic is read-only single-pass (critic-protocol AX_READ_ONLY); the ROOT session owns the round loop, reuse-reconciliation (STEP_2B), accept/reject, and ALL edits. If a critic returns applied edits or a multi-round report, treat it as overreach: keep only its findings, discard the rest, run STEP_2→5 yourself.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_NO_RE_DISPATCH">Substantive edits after a non-CLEAN verdict without focused verification. Such an edit invalidates the prior verdict.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_SPIN">Re-dispatch with zero edits. Same input → same verdict.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_POLISH_SPIN">Re-dispatching after any CLEAN verdict to re-validate optional MINOR polish. CLEAN is terminal (AX_CLEAN_TERMINAL).</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_OVEREDIT">Rewriting sections. Close the gap, don't redecorate.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_CONFUSION_TO_EDIT">Treating every "I don't understand X" as an artifact defect. Classify it through AX_CONFUSION_TRIAGE first.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_VAGUE_REJECT">Rejecting without citing specific context.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_ENTITY_SPRAWL">Accepting a new entity/type/method implicated by a finding without first searching the project for one to reuse or extend. New surface every round = sprawl.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_PHANTOM_ACCEPT">Accepting an additive finding (new error-kind, Result wrapper, param, dependency) without naming the real failure it guards. Cancellation/dispose/abort is not a failure (AX_NECESSITY_FIRST).</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_COAUTHOR">Using critique to add requirements, compare alternative designs, improve completeness, or rewrite neighboring artifacts. Critic closes evidence-backed gaps in the current artifact only.</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_NEW_FRONTIER">Running a fresh full audit after round 1 or folding an unrelated late concern into the active loop. Verification rounds stay on the accepted-fix frontier (AX_ROUND_FRONTIER).</Pattern>
    <Pattern id="AP_CROSS_ARTIFACT_EDIT">Editing parent spec, DAG, sibling tasks, or conventions while critiquing one artifact (AX_ARTIFACT_BOUNDARY).</Pattern>
  </AntiPatterns>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="0_RESOLVE">
      <Goal>Resolve what to critique.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Operator input → determine scope:
        - .spec.md path → ask: (1) spec only, (2) spec + all tasks, (3) all tasks only.
        - .task-*.md path → single task, no question.
        - scope name / tasks/<scope>/ → all tasks in scope.
        Build queue: spec-first if included, then tasks in DAG layers.
        For each task: read §1 Meta → resolve parent spec. Missing → H_PARENT_SPEC_MISSING.
        Determine polish-mode (AX_POLISH_MODE): operator asked to "шлифуй" / "и мелочи" / "polish" / "nits" → ON; otherwise OFF (default — CRITICAL/MAJOR only).
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="1_DISPATCH">
      <Goal>Dispatch one isolated critic subagent.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Dispatch subagent (`subagent_type: general-purpose`) in fresh context. Do not pin a model;
        inherit the caller's configured model because critic quality is part of the active runtime
        policy, not this directive:
        ```
        Step 1 — Read directive: ai/directives/sdd/critic-protocol.xml
        Step 2 — Activate. Announce: "🔒 SddCriticProtocol"
        Step 3 — Apply. Artifact: <absolute-path>, Parent spec: <absolute-path|N/A>, Round: <N>, Review mode: <baseline|verification>, Polish: <on|off>.
        Previous accepted findings: <N/A|list>.
        Changed sections since previous round: <N/A|list>.
        Follow ExecutionPlan. Do not deviate.

        HARD CONSTRAINTS — override any contrary impulse:
        - READ-ONLY. Do NOT edit/create/delete ANY file (not the artifact, not specs, nothing). The root orchestrator owns every edit.
        - SINGLE PASS. Run the protocol ONCE for THIS round only. Do NOT run multiple rounds, do NOT re-dispatch, do NOT "helpfully" apply or implement fixes.
        - OUTPUT = the four report sections + Verdict, then STOP. Returning edits or a multi-round report is a protocol violation, not helpfulness.
        ```
        Fail → retry once. Fail again → H_DISPATCH_FAILED.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="2_EVALUATE">
      <Goal>Classify findings: ACCEPT or REJECT.</Goal>
      <Action>
        ACCEPT: evidence-backed artifact gap that passes AX_FINDING_EVIDENCE and can be closed surgically in the current artifact.
        REJECT as blocking: preference, alternative design, uncertainty without evidence, missing local context, or a misreading resolved by specific project context (AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT, AX_CONFUSION_TRIAGE).
        ADDITIVE finding (demands new surface) → apply AX_NECESSITY_FIRST: accept ONLY if you can name the concrete failure it guards; cancellation/dispose/abort is not a failure → REJECT and keep the surface minimal.
        Confusion points → classify ARTIFACT_GAP | CONTEXT_MISSING | NON_BLOCKING_QUESTION (AX_CONFUSION_TRIAGE). Only ARTIFACT_GAP enters ACCEPT/REJECT.
        In verification mode, a new independent concern outside previous findings and changed sections → H_AUTHORING_REQUIRED after recording it; do not edit it inside this loop (AX_ROUND_FRONTIER).
        `## Язык (не блокирует)` hits (AX_LANGUAGE_REGISTER_CHANNEL in critic-protocol) → apply as surgical wording edits by default (quote → replacement, meaning untouched); they never count toward the verdict and never justify a re-dispatch on their own.
        Go to STEP_2B only for accepted findings that introduce or change surface. Otherwise go to STEP_3 with accepted non-surface gaps, or STEP_5 when there are no edits.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="2B_RECONCILE">
      <Goal>Reuse-first reconciliation — orchestrator-only, uses full project context (AX_REUSE_FIRST).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Reconcile only the entity/type/method/contract implicated by an accepted finding. Never inventory every surface in the artifact during critique.
        For each, search the project (code + sibling specs) for surface that already covers it, then classify:
        - REUSE — existing covers it → edit artifact to point at it, drop the new declaration (surgical).
        - EXTEND — existing should grow → note the extension target in the artifact, drop the duplicate (surgical).
        - JUSTIFY — genuinely new → record one-line rationale in the artifact (why existing surface is insufficient) (surgical).
        - ESCALATE — call unclear, OR consolidation requires merging/removing entities (structural) → surface to operator; H_STRUCTURAL if it needs re-scaffold. Do NOT perform structural consolidation yourself.
        Surgical reuse/justify edits + accepted findings → go to STEP_3. Zero edits after reconciliation → go to STEP_5 (stop).
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="3_EDIT">
      <Goal>Surgical edit.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per accepted finding: add a required missing BDD scenario, clarify the ambiguous boundary, correct the conflicting entity ref, or fill a blocking placeholder. Per reconcile decision: point at existing surface (REUSE/EXTEND) or record new-entity rationale (JUSTIFY). Target only the gap in the current artifact. A parent-spec/DAG/sibling edit → H_AUTHORING_REQUIRED. Structural rewrite or entity merge/removal → H_STRUCTURAL / ESCALATE.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="4_RECORD">
      <Goal>Append scratch log.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Create/append `## Critic Rounds`:
        ```
        ### Round N — YYYY-MM-DD
        - Mode: <baseline|verification>
        - Verdict: <CLEAN|NEEDS_WORK|CRITICAL>
        - Accepted: N — <list>
        - Rejected: N — "<finding>" → <reason>
        - Context: <CONTEXT_MISSING items resolved by orchestrator | none>
        - Reconcile: <entity → REUSE <target> | EXTEND <target> | JUSTIFY <rationale> | ESCALATE>
        - Changes: <list>
        ```
        Append-only.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="5_DECIDE">
      <Goal>Re-dispatch or conclude.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Verdict CLEAN → conclude immediately (go to STEP_6), regardless of round number or optional MINOR wording edits (AX_CLEAN_TERMINAL).
        No edits → conclude (go to STEP_6).
        Same mechanism received substantive findings in two consecutive rounds → H_AUTHORING_REQUIRED (AX_SAME_MECHANISM_STOP).
        SUBSTANTIVE edits applied AND round < 5 → round++, set Review mode = verification, pass accepted findings + changed sections, go to STEP_1 (AX_RE_DISPATCH, AX_ROUND_FRONTIER).
        Round 5 → conclude, flag MAX_ROUNDS if not CLEAN.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="6_FINALIZE">
      <Goal>Cleanup and detailed final summary.</Goal>
      <Action>
        If final critic verdict CLEAN → replace the detailed `## Critic Rounds` body with:
        ```markdown
        ## Critic Rounds

        @critic status=CLEAN rounds=<N> final-round=<N> date=<YYYY-MM-DD>
        ```
        If not CLEAN → keep detailed round entries as documentation of unresolved findings.

        Emit FULL summary (operator needs detail to discuss, challenge, or revert):
        ```
        🔍 sdd-critic — <path>

        📊 Rounds: N
          R1: <verdict>
            🔴 CRITICAL: <N>  🟠 MAJOR: <N>  🟡 MINOR: <N>  🔵 INFO: <N>
            Принято:
              - <finding summary> → <what was changed>
              - ...
            Отклонено:
              - "<finding summary>" → <reason (specific context)>
              - ...

          R2: <verdict>
            (same structure)
            ...

          RN: <verdict> → <stop reason>

        ✏️ All changes:
          - <change>
          - ...

        ♻️ Reuse decisions:
          - <entity> → REUSE <target> | EXTEND <target> | JUSTIFY <rationale> | ESCALATE <question>
          - ...

        ⚠️ Unresolved (if not CLEAN):
          - <finding> → <recommendation>

        📍 Artifact: <path> — <CLEAN | NEEDS_WORK | CRITICAL>
        ```

        Then the handoff menu per `NEXT_STEP_MENU_FORMAT` (`ai/directives/sdd/interview-protocol.xml`) — one AskUserQuestion, never text «запусти /sdd-X». Candidates by artifact kind:
        - scope spec (product/library) → «Декомпозиция на модули (рекомендую)» · «Scaffold + критик» · «Закончить сессию»;
        - scope spec (infrastructure/contracts) or module specs → «Scaffold + критик (рекомендую)» · «Сразу scaffold» · «Закончить сессию»;
        - task ticket(s) → «Выполнить (sdd-execute) (рекомендую)» · «Выполнить всю очередь (sdd-execute-batch)» · «Закончить сессию».
        Not CLEAN without a halt → prepend «Показать нерешённые находки и решить вручную (рекомендую)» and demote the pipeline options.
        MAX_ROUNDS / H_STRUCTURAL / H_AUTHORING_REQUIRED → do NOT offer execution, scaffold, or another critic pass. Offer only «Вернуться к авторингу и изменить дизайн (рекомендую)» · «Показать нерешённые находки» · «Закончить сессию». A later critic run is a new baseline only after an explicit authoring change, never a reset of the same loop.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <HardForbidden>
    - Self-critique. Dispatch critic.
    - Re-dispatch with zero edits.
    - Re-dispatch after any CLEAN verdict (AX_CLEAN_TERMINAL) — CLEAN concludes the loop.
    - >5 rounds.
    - Reset/restart the same critic loop after MAX_ROUNDS without an explicit separate authoring change.
    - Rewrite artifact.
    - Share full context with critic.
    - Run a broad baseline audit after round 1; verification rounds stay on changed sections and accepted findings.
    - Accept uncertainty, CONTEXT_MISSING, or a design preference as a blocking finding.
    - Edit parent spec, DAG, sibling tasks, or project conventions while reviewing one artifact.
    - Delete all evidence of a CLEAN critic run; keep the compact final `@critic` record.
    - ACCEPT without edit.
    - REJECT without specific context.
    - Accept a new entity without reuse-first reconciliation (AX_REUSE_FIRST).
    - Reconcile every entity in the artifact without an accepted finding implicating it.
    - Accept an additive finding without naming the concrete failure it guards (AX_NECESSITY_FIRST).
    - Structurally merge/remove entities yourself — ESCALATE instead.
  </HardForbidden>
</SddCritic>
